    "result": "No test directory exists in this checkout, so nothing to run locally beyond my manual check, which confirmed the fix.\n\nThe regression was in `sqlparse/tokens.py`'s `_TokenType.__getattr__`: it had a comment \"don't mess with dunder\" but no actual check, so dunder attribute lookups (like `__deepcopy__`, `__copy__`, `__reduce_ex__`) returned new `_TokenType` instances instead of raising `AttributeError`. This broke `copy.deepcopy()`/`copy.copy()` on tokens/statements, since Python's copy machinery would find a truthy `__deepcopy__` attribute and try to call it, hitting `TypeError: '_TokenType' object is not callable`. Added the missing dunder guard to raise `AttributeError` for dunder names, restoring correct `copy`/`deepcopy` behavior while leaving normal token attribute access unchanged."
  },
